# Git & PR Conventions

- Branches: `<type>/<short-description>` (e.g. `feat/vendor-invoices`, `fix/deploy-migration-order`).
- Commits: imperative mood, explain _why_, not just _what_.
- PRs: state what changed, why, and how it was tested.
- Call out explicitly if a change touches deploy or migration behavior — reviewers
  should look harder at that category.
- Write down decisions of consequence (schema changes, a new dependency, a real
  tradeoff) in the PR description at minimum, not only in chat.
